<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alcide De Gasperi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1881–1954</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alcide De Gasperi was an Italian statesman, founder of the Christian Democracy party, and prime minister from 1945 to 1953. He led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> through the transition from monarchy to republic in 1946, anchored it in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marshall-plan">Marshall Plan</a>, and was one of the founders of European integration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alcide-de-gasperi.jpg" alt="Alcide De Gasperi" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alcide_de_Gasperi_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
